cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "jev-tune: a calibrated decision and safety-shell reference with a PID testbed"
message: "If you use this software, please cite this version (and, once a DOI is minted, the archived release it points to)."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Jiawei"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/lijiawei255/jev-tune"
url: "https://github.com/lijiawei255/jev-tune"
abstract: >-
  A decomposable calibrated decision and safety-shell reference with PID
  and non-PID simulation testbeds. Each decision is a typed judgement
  (choice / score / noul) produced by a small numeric head,
  instead of an autoregressive language-model call. The project borrows Jev's
  interface (TypeSafe AI) and none of its weights, text encoder or API; it is
  not affiliated with TypeSafe AI. Ships a Python simulator, a Simulink bridge
  that runs the head inside MATLAB, an MCP server, a documented benchmark at a
  common experiment budget, and a limitations document that includes the
  negative results.
keywords:
  - PID tuning
  - control engineering
  - Simulink
  - MATLAB
  - typed decisions
  - Jev-inspired
  - ONNX
  - CPU inference
version: 0.10.1
